# issues/fixed/interior-ref-arg-borrow-acquire-never-emitted.md: an element of
# a container passed as an `inout` argument (`bump(xs(usize(0)))`) acquires the
# RC header's borrow flag on `xs` for the call; the callee reaches `xs` through
# a module-level structure the static place rule cannot see and grows it, and
# `push` must PANIC ("container operation while an interior reference ...
# borrows from it") instead of reallocating the buffer the reference points
# into. The program compiles cleanly and panics at run time; `build run`
# propagates that as a non-zero rc. The panic rides stderr with build chatter,
# so stdout keeps only the diagnostic substring.
stdout_keep_match=panic: container operation while an interior reference.*
timeout=300
